{"message":"Thanks — I can proceed. To verify your identity I need two pieces of information. Please provide: 1) either the email on your Rho account OR your full name (case-sensitive) so I can look you up, AND 2) one additional verification field: date of birth (MM/DD/YYYY), phone number, or your address. 

Also — is the teen account card registered to your daughter under your profile (i.e., are you the guardian on that Light Green/teen account)?

Once you provide those, I’ll verify and look up your cards and limits/status right away."}

{"message":"Thanks — quickest fix is a 24-hour temporary ATM limit increase on your Green card. Quick summary: based on today’s posted withdrawals from your Green account you’ve already taken out about $350, leaving roughly $250 available of the $600 daily ATM limit. That’s why the $550 attempt was declined (it exceeded your remaining daily ATM allowance).

I can request a temporary increase now. Rules/notes: the temporary boost lasts 24 hours and can raise the ATM limit up to 150% of the current limit (Green’s current ATM limit = $600 → maximum temporary limit = $900). Also, Rho cannot override a third‑party ATM’s internal per‑transaction cap; if that convenience‑store ATM has a lower per‑transaction limit, the withdrawal could still be declined — so if possible I recommend using a Rho ATM or a branch teller after I raise the limit.

Would you like me to request a temporary ATM limit increase to $900 on your Green card (dbc_2f8a7c3d1e9b) now? If you prefer a smaller increase, tell me the new limit you want (must be ≤ $900). If you want me to proceed, say “Yes — raise to $900.”"}
